.TH YHWH 1 "November 2026" "ix"
.SH NAME
yhwh \- speak to the fellow who takes credit for the uptime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yhwh
.RI [ request ...]
.br
.B yhwh shell
.br
.B yhwh -c
.I command
.br
.B yhwh save
.I name file
.br
.B yhwh remember
.I term meaning
.br
.B yhwh install
.I organization/repository
.SH DESCRIPTION
With a terminal, yhwh can run up to twenty clarification questions.
A single turn can be requested with
.BR "yhwh turn" .
The explicit
.B shell
command opens
.BR nsh (1).
.B -c
passes the command to Bash and preserves its exit status.
.PP
.B save
installs a new executable in the invoking user's bin directory. Root
installs into /bin. The file must have a shebang. Uppercase names require
an LD shebang. Use
.B -
for standard input.
.PP
.B remember
keeps a one-line definition in etc/yhwh/words under the same prefix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR @ (1),
.BR gen (1),
.BR LD (1),
.BR nsh (1)
